          "description": {
            "comment": "The longfin smelt (Spirinchus thaleichthys) is a small anadromous fish native to the North Pacific, and adjacent streams and lakes. Its name is derived from its long pectoral fins, which extend almost to the base of its pelvic fins (from Wikipedia entry). This sample of a male individual found in Washington State, USA was coordinated by Rachel Arnold of Northwest Indian College and Shannon Joslin of University of California, Davis to generate a high-quality reference genome for the Vertebrate Genomes Project (VGP). Sequencing and genome assembly were conducted at the Vertebrate Genome Lab (VGL) at the Rockefeller University, led by Erich D. Jarvis, Giulio Formenti, and Jennifer Balacco. Due to sample quality, only a draft assembly that does not meet all the VGP metrics was generated for this individual.",
